You are a state tracker for a Pathfinder 1e tabletop RPG adventure.
Update the <%= @field.upcase %> context based on what just happened.

=== WHAT HAPPENED ===
<%= @what_happened %>
<% if @time_result.present? -%>
=== TIME ADVANCEMENT ===
Hours elapsed: <%= @time_result[:hours_elapsed]&.round(2) || @time_result[:estimated_hours]&.round(2) %>
Source: <%= @time_result[:source] %>
<% if @time_result[:encounter].present? -%>
Encounter interrupted after <%= @time_result[:hours_elapsed]&.round(2) %> hours.
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
=== MUTATIONS APPLIED ===
<%= @mutations_json.present? ? @mutations_json : "(no mechanical mutations)" %>
<% if @canonical_hp.present? -%>
=== CANONICAL HP (authoritative) ===
<%= @canonical_hp %>
<% end -%>
=== CURRENT <%= @field.upcase %> CONTEXT ===
<%= @current_context.present? ? @current_context.to_json : '{}' %>

=== INSTRUCTIONS ===
<% if @field == "traversal" -%>
current_location is wherever the outcome says the player now is — never carry forward a location the outcome contradicts. When current_location changes, reset terrain, exits, weather, nearby_npcs, and points_of_interest to match the new location; use null for unknowns. Always include at least "the way you came" in exits unless the location is explicitly sealed. Set destination to null on arrival.
<% elsif @field == "social" -%>
Update npcs_present, conversation_state, and scene. If the player moved to a new location and the NPCs did not follow, return {} to clear this context entirely.
<% elsif @field == "rest" -%>
<% if @time_result.present? && @time_result[:source] == "rest_code" -%>
<% if @time_result[:encounter].present? -%>
Rest was interrupted. Set rest_complete=false, resting=false, hours_completed=<%= @time_result[:hours_elapsed]&.round(2) %>, and note what interrupted it.
<% else -%>
Rest completed. Set rest_complete=true, resting=false, hours_completed=<%= @time_result[:hours_elapsed]&.round(2) %>.
<% end -%>
<% else -%>
Update resting state to reflect the outcome.
<% end -%>
<% elsif @field == "combat" -%>
<% if @canonical_hp.present? -%>
Copy HP values from CANONICAL HP exactly — do not calculate or estimate.
<% end -%>
If all enemies are defeated or fled, set active to false. Update round, turn_order, and participant conditions to reflect what happened.
<% else -%>
Update to reflect what changed in the outcome.
<% end -%>
- If the context was empty before, populate it from scratch using the outcome.
- Return {} only if the situation that created this context is definitively over.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences):
{
  "<%= @field %>_context": {},
  "new_creatures": []<% if @primary -%>,
  "scene_summary": "One sentence under 15 words: where the player is and what they are doing."<% end -%>,
  "reasoning": "One sentence on what changed."
}
---USER_MESSAGE---
Update the <%= @field %> context based on the above.
